        Root cause:
        The bug is a race condition between dquot_scan_active() and quota deactivation (quota_release_workfn()). dquot_scan_active() iterates over the inuse_list and increments dq_count (via atomic_inc) without checking whether the dquot has been moved to the releasing list (where dq_count == 0 but DQ_ACTIVE_B is still set). This allows a reference to be taken on a dquot that is about to be freed, leading to a WARN_ON and potential use-after-free. The fix introduces __dqgrab() which, under dq_list_lock, removes the dquot from the releasing list if its count is zero before incrementing.

        Commit message:
        quota: Fix race of dquot_scan_active() with quota
 deactivation

dquot_scan_active() can race with quota deactivation in
quota_release_workfn() like:

  CPU0 (quota_release_workfn)         CPU1 (dquot_scan_active)
  ==============================      ==============================
  spin_lock(&dq_list_lock);
  list_replace_init(
    &releasing_dquots, &rls_head);
    /* dquot X on rls_head,
       dq_count == 0,
       DQ_ACTIVE_B still set */
  spin_unlock(&dq_list_lock);
  synchronize_srcu(&dquot_srcu);
